But Roy is like, I mean, you called off our wedding for the guy.

1636
01:16:14.010 --> 01:16:15.770
And now you're not going to date him?

1637
01:16:15.850 --> 01:16:17.010
I just don't get you, Pam.

1638
01:16:17.970 --> 01:16:20.110
Well, he calls you Pammy.

1639
01:16:20.750 --> 01:16:29.990
And you also say, well, there were other reasons too, which I think is Pam just being polite and not saying you did this.

1640
01:16:29.990 --> 01:16:30.870
You didn't do this.

1641
01:16:30.990 --> 01:16:35.270
She doesn't want to run him, you know, through the ringer and just leaves it at that.

1642
01:16:35.530 --> 01:16:43.870
But I do think that Roy saying that is planting the seed for what Pam's going to do.

1643
01:16:45.070 --> 01:16:45.590
Later.

1644
01:16:46.750 --> 01:16:47.870
Because it's true.

1645
01:16:48.490 --> 01:16:49.190
It's true.

1646
01:16:49.490 --> 01:16:54.670
She did call off her wedding to Roy in part because she had feelings for Jim.

1647
01:16:54.810 --> 01:17:02.050
If she did not have feelings for Jim, I'm not sure she would have called off the wedding just because they were not a perfect match.

1648
01:17:02.050 --> 01:17:03.050
I agree.

1649
01:17:03.270 --> 01:17:12.010
I think her feelings for Jim and the way Jim sort of held up a mirror to her life changed her.

1650
01:17:12.150 --> 01:17:14.170
And he is the reason.

1651
01:17:14.470 --> 01:17:16.310
He's a big, big part of the reason.

1652
01:17:16.670 --> 01:17:16.850
Yeah.

1653
01:17:18.860 --> 01:17:19.480
All right.

1654
01:17:19.740 --> 01:17:22.200
Well, that was we talked about this with David a little bit.

1655
01:17:22.340 --> 01:17:23.880
That was a really special scene for me.

1656
01:17:24.000 --> 01:17:25.420
I love doing that scene with him.

1657
01:17:25.620 --> 01:17:27.360
I just love doing scenes with David.

1658
01:17:27.580 --> 01:17:28.640
He was a great actor.

1659
01:17:28.820 --> 01:17:30.200
He's a great acting partner.

1660
01:17:31.280 --> 01:17:37.900
And I was really sad knowing that that was, you know, going to be the last scene we would do for a while.

1661
01:17:38.420 --> 01:17:39.160
I know.

1662
01:17:39.460 --> 01:17:40.940
You guys had a really special thing.

1663
01:17:40.940 --> 01:17:44.180
And I loved being able to watch that scene.

1664
01:17:44.180 --> 01:17:51.780
He was kind of the first major regular character who had been with us from the beginning who was leaving the show.

1665
01:17:52.620 --> 01:17:53.100
Yes.

1666
01:17:53.640 --> 01:17:54.120
Yes.

1667
01:17:54.380 --> 01:17:56.460
And that was we'd been through a lot.

1668
01:17:56.640 --> 01:17:59.260
You know, he was part of our origin story.

1669
01:17:59.500 --> 01:18:01.760
He was with us when the show was struggling.

1670
01:18:01.760 --> 01:18:04.460
And then he was with us when we started getting awards.

1671
01:18:04.460 --> 01:18:06.400
And it was really weird to say goodbye.

1672
01:18:07.360 --> 01:18:07.640
Yeah.

1673
01:18:09.380 --> 01:18:16.100
Well, lady, we should go back to corporate because we've got some unfinished business there.

1674
01:18:16.440 --> 01:18:19.460
Michael and Jan are in the throes of negotiation.

1675
01:18:20.300 --> 01:18:24.200
And he says, give me a raise or no more sex.

1676
01:18:24.460 --> 01:18:26.000
And Toby just starts taking notes.

